  "verbalization": "Isotretinoin is associated with Rarb through a mechanistic pathway involving retinoic acid signaling. The evidence suggests that Isotretinoin, a retinoic acid agent, causes various clinical effects such as decreased night vision, skin fragility, and hyperostosis, all of which are mediated by Acitretin, a metabolite of Isotretinoin. Acitretin binds to Rarb, a receptor involved in retinoic acid signaling, thereby modulating its activity. This binding is consistent with the observed effects of Isotretinoin on Rarb, indicating a direct interaction between the drug and the receptor. The presence of a common ancestor in the pathway—Retinoic Acid Agent and Retinoid—supports the role of Rarb in the downstream effects of retinoic acid. The integrated evidence suggests that Isotretinoin exerts its effects on Rarb through retinoic acid signaling, with Acitretin serving as a critical mediator in this process. The relationship is supported by multiple paths with high scores, indicating a robust and well-documented mechanism.",
